# Generated data, not hand-authored -- see data/README.md for what's
# committed (data/synthetic_logs.jsonl, the canonical corpus) vs. what
# regenerates from the fixed seed and doesn't need to be tracked.
data/raw/
data/load_test_corpus_*.jsonl
data/validate_corpus.jsonl

# Load-test run artifacts (validation/load_test/README.md) -- timestamped
# logs/summaries from each local run, not meant to accumulate in git.
validation/load_test/results/

# Real US name-frequency source data (ROADMAP item 10) -- downloaded fresh
# via validation/real_name_frequency/download_name_data.sh, same pattern
# as validation/real_data/'s Loghub logs (*.log, already ignored above),
# not checked into the repo.
validation/real_name_frequency/raw/*.zip

# One-off 100K-line synthetic corpus generated for the field-gated
# throughput follow-up (run_100k_throughput_check.sh) -- same fixed-seed
# regeneration pattern as data/load_test_corpus_*.jsonl above, not the
# canonical corpus (data/synthetic_logs.jsonl), so it doesn't need to be
# tracked either.
data/synthetic_logs_100k.jsonl

# Generated corpus for run_replica_and_queue_test.sh (ROADMAP item 12) --
# same fixed-seed regeneration pattern as the load-test corpora above.
data/replica_queue_test_corpus_*.jsonl

# Generated corpus for run_redis_failover_test.sh (Bug 22/23/24) -- same
# fixed-seed regeneration pattern. Missed when that script was first
# added (found here, fixed the same way every other stale/missing bit of
# housekeeping in this project gets caught -- by noticing it, not by
# leaving it for later).
data/redis_failover_test_corpus_*.jsonl

# Generated corpus for run_floci_kafka_test.sh (ROADMAP item 13) -- same
# fixed-seed regeneration pattern as the other run_*_test.sh corpora
# above. Added proactively this time, not found missing after the fact
# (see Bug 22/23/24's own corpus-gitignore-gap history above).
data/kafka_queue_test_corpus_*.jsonl

# CloudTrailFlaws_raw.jsonl (validation/real_data/prepare_cloudtrail_dataset.py)
# -- regenerable from the public flaws.cloud release, same pattern as the
# Loghub *.log files above (already covered by *.log; this one is .jsonl
# so needs its own line). The 240MB source .tar it's derived from must
# never be committed under any circumstance -- caught and reverted the one
# time this almost happened, 2026-08-10, see BUGS_AND_FIXES.md if it
# recurs. Real accident, not a hypothetical: `git add -A` after running
# prepare_cloudtrail_dataset.py picked up both the .tar and this file
# before this rule existed.
validation/real_data/datasets/CloudTrailFlaws_raw.jsonl
*.tar
